    <string name="player_privacy_body">Local playback and music library\nThe standalone player opens media through Android MediaStore access or files you explicitly select. Audio and video library permissions are optional; selected files can be opened without broad library access. Local playback and subtitles use content-provider access, not direct network streaming. A cloud document provider may retrieve a selected file under its own privacy practices.\n\nFavorites, playback playlists, the last playback queue, resume positions and player options are saved in app-private storage. Selected file references may retain the read access you grant for later playback. These records are not uploaded to a MediaFlow service. You can remove favorites, delete playback playlists or clear the queue in the player. Removing a playback reference does not delete the original media file. Android settings controls media access; uninstalling removes app-private playback records.</string>
